WEBVTT

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:39.198
It's extraordinary.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.504
I must remind you

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:45.238
that it is also
a potential security risk.

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:48.406
It's losing power.

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:49.710
I'd like to move it
to Engineering

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.547
to see if I can repair it
before it drains completely.

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:54.849
I suggest we allow
the power to drain.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:58.551
We should take the opportunity
to examine it while it is idle.

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:01.287
Then we can decide
whether it is wise to repair it.

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:03.352
Captain, this thing

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:05.057
has a completely
unfamiliar power source.

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:06.690
Once it stops working,

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:09.065
it's very possible I'll never
be able to get it going again

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.660
and we'll have lost
an opportunity

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.796
to study a new technology.

00:01:12.839 --> 00:01:16.366
This is a ship of exploration,
Mr. Tuvok.

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.104
The power's surging.

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:26.282
If we can't find
a way to stabilize it,

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.116
we're going to lose it.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:31.920
What about an interface
with an EPS power conduit?

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.654
Well, the energy signatures
are incompatible, but...

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.924
it might buy us some time.

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:49.099
Okay, let's give it a try.

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:52.703
Two-second burst,
five percent maximum output.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.847
On my mark.

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:57.509
Now.

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.417
We're losing it.

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.580
Maybe we're overloading
its systems.

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:04.954
Let's try a longer
burst at lower power.

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:06.116
Got it.

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:08.093
Five seconds at three percent.

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:09.425
On your mark.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:11.293
Now.

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:12.730
I think it's working.

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.926
EPS flow is holding steady.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.959
EM field leakage is minimal.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.561
We'll have to watch
the pressure at the connector.

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:22.439
Let's try to keep it
below 85 percent.

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:25.342
Flux capacitance is spiking
intermittently,

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:27.141
but I don't think
that's the problem.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.148
Let's reinforce the
power conduit coupling,

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:31.173
just to be on the safe side.

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:21.956
It's suffered a lot of damage...

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.358
but I think the EPS charge

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:26.297
will keep it running
for at least 18 hours.

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:27.959
It's not a cyborg.

00:04:28.034 --> 00:04:29.763
It's completely robotic.

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:31.770
No organic components
of any kind.

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:35.831
This looks like some kind
of programming center.

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:37.536
But I'm not detecting
any pathways

00:04:37.577 --> 00:04:39.909
for transmitting information.

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:41.379
It's got arms, legs.

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:43.245
We saw it move its head.

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:46.741
It's clearly designed
to perform motor functions...

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:49.186
so where do
those commands come from?

00:04:49.222 --> 00:04:52.988
Maybe it needs to interface
with an outside source.

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:54.653
Speaking of sources,

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:58.255
this energy module
seems to be what powers

00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:00.163
the entire mechanism.

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:03.726
It isn't designed
to run on EPS energy.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:07.934
It runs on some kind of
superconducting plasma.

00:05:07.974 --> 00:05:12.502
If we keep charging it,
we may end up destroying it.

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:19.876
It's trying to communicate.

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:21.045
We don't know that.

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:22.588
It may just be
some kind of recording.

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:24.556
Pralor... Pralor...

00:05:25.891 --> 00:05:26.915
Pralor... Pralor... Pralor...

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.824
Pralor... Pralor...
Pralor...

00:05:30.262 --> 00:05:31.889
What are you trying to say?

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:34.694
What's Pralor?

00:05:34.733 --> 00:05:38.669
If you can hear me,
try to move...

00:05:38.704 --> 00:05:40.103
try to move your arm.

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:47.167
B'Elanna, we don't even know
if it can see you,

00:05:47.212 --> 00:05:51.012
much less understand
a word you're saying.

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:06.921
We've got to figure out
a way to fix it.

00:06:06.999 --> 00:06:08.296
We've been trying for hours.

00:06:08.333 --> 00:06:09.630
We need a break.

00:06:09.668 --> 00:06:11.761
The EPS charge should
hold till morning.

00:06:11.803 --> 00:06:13.100
You go ahead.

00:06:13.138 --> 00:06:15.936
I could use some time
alone to think.

00:06:15.974 --> 00:06:18.306
If you're staying, I'm staying.

00:06:18.343 --> 00:06:19.935
Get some rest, Harry.

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:22.037
You may think you're tougher

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.480
than everybody else,
B'Elanna Torres,

00:06:24.516 --> 00:06:27.485
but I can go without sleep
just as long as you can.

00:06:27.519 --> 00:06:30.181
Don't make me laugh, Starfleet.

00:06:30.222 --> 00:06:33.885
And don't make me
pull rank on you, either.

00:06:33.925 --> 00:06:35.222
If you insist.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:38.787
But let me know if you
come up with anything...

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.195
Lieutenant.

00:06:47.939 --> 00:06:50.533
Chief Engineer's Log,
supplemental.

00:06:50.575 --> 00:06:52.440
I've tried 13 different methods

00:06:52.477 --> 00:06:54.968
of reinitializing
the robot's power source

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:56.775
and I'm still having no luck.

00:06:56.815 --> 00:06:58.976
So I've decided
to go to the Mess Hall

00:06:59.084 --> 00:07:01.848
to recharge my own
declining energy reserves.

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:16.361
Neelix, I need
another pot of coffee.

00:07:16.401 --> 00:07:19.666
Even though breakfast
isn't officially served

00:07:19.705 --> 00:07:21.138
for another hour and a half,

00:07:21.173 --> 00:07:24.939
I'd be happy to pour you
a glass of Traggle nectar.

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:26.944
I will even fix you

00:07:27.045 --> 00:07:29.809
my special Jibalian
seven-spice omelette.

00:07:29.848 --> 00:07:31.145
Just coffee.

00:07:31.183 --> 00:07:32.946
I'm sorry, B'Elanna,

00:07:33.051 --> 00:07:34.416
but two pots of Landras blend

00:07:34.453 --> 00:07:37.547
is the absolute limit.

00:07:37.589 --> 00:07:39.386
You're cutting me off?

00:07:44.129 --> 00:07:46.689
Oh, I guess you're right.

00:07:46.732 --> 00:07:49.963
It was starting
to taste almost palatable.

00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:56.600
Still no idea how to revive
our mechanized guest?

00:07:56.641 --> 00:08:00.441
All I've been able to do
is postpone the inevitable.

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:06.418
The constant power depletion
is like a bleeding artery...

00:08:06.451 --> 00:08:08.851
and I haven't got a tourniquet.

00:08:08.887 --> 00:08:10.912
I remember when I was trying

00:08:10.956 --> 00:08:14.483
to perfect the recipe
for my Jibalian omelette.

00:08:14.526 --> 00:08:15.925
I tried everything...

00:08:16.027 --> 00:08:19.656
a little more Spith basil,
a little less prishic...

00:08:19.698 --> 00:08:21.791
but I couldn't get it right.

00:08:21.833 --> 00:08:24.700
Finally, I fell asleep
from exhaustion.

00:08:24.736 --> 00:08:27.330
Right there at the counter.

00:08:27.372 --> 00:08:30.739
And then, in a dream,
it came to me.

00:08:30.776 --> 00:08:35.907
I was using six spices,
but the omelette needed seven.

00:08:35.947 --> 00:08:37.608
Let me guess.

00:08:37.649 --> 00:08:39.207
Leola root.

00:08:39.251 --> 00:08:42.482
Nimian sea salt, actually.

00:08:42.521 --> 00:08:43.488
Salt?

00:08:43.522 --> 00:08:44.614
Yes, salt...

00:08:44.656 --> 00:08:47.454
the most common spice
in the galaxy.

00:08:47.492 --> 00:08:50.791
But I was too tired,
so I couldn't see it.

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:54.428
That is...

00:08:54.466 --> 00:08:57.629
a very interesting
story, Neelix.

00:08:57.669 --> 00:09:00.502
Now, how about some more coffee?

00:09:00.539 --> 00:09:02.769
To bed.

00:09:03.141 --> 00:09:04.870
I said to bed.

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:05.899
I'm going.

00:09:08.747 --> 00:09:09.736
I'm going.

00:09:27.966 --> 00:09:29.957
Anybody home?

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:33.895
What's that?

00:09:33.939 --> 00:09:37.170
You think I should
go to bed, too?

00:09:40.045 --> 00:09:42.240
Well...

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:44.874
I guess I'm outnumbered.

00:10:15.714 --> 00:10:19.707
Computer, activate emergency
medical holographic program.

00:10:19.751 --> 00:10:21.309
Please state the nature...

00:10:24.289 --> 00:10:26.484
If there has been a change
in the official dress code,

00:10:26.524 --> 00:10:28.389
I certainly wish someone
would've informed me.

00:10:28.426 --> 00:10:29.723
This is what I sleep in.

00:10:29.761 --> 00:10:31.285
I didn't have time to change.

00:10:31.329 --> 00:10:32.853
I see.

00:10:32.898 --> 00:10:34.388
May I assume your haste
is an indication

00:10:34.432 --> 00:10:36.229
that you have a medical
problem of some kind?

00:10:36.268 --> 00:10:38.702
An engineering problem,
actually,

00:10:38.737 --> 00:10:39.704
but I thought you
might have some insight.

00:10:39.738 --> 00:10:41.603
Hmm...

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:43.631
I shouldn't have
to remind you I'm a doctor...

00:10:43.675 --> 00:10:44.869
Not an engineer.
Right.

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:47.003
But this isn't a typical
engineering problem.

00:10:47.112 --> 00:10:51.139
I've been working on trying
to repair a robot.

00:10:51.182 --> 00:10:53.013
Ah, yes.
The mechanical man.

00:10:53.118 --> 00:10:54.551
Kes told me about it.

00:10:54.586 --> 00:10:55.553
Fascinating.

00:10:55.587 --> 00:10:56.884
He's about to die.

00:10:56.922 --> 00:10:57.889
Die?

00:10:57.923 --> 00:10:58.890
Die. Stop functioning.
Whatever.

00:10:58.924 --> 00:11:00.414
Unless I can figure out
a way

00:11:00.458 --> 00:11:02.255
to sustain
his main energy source.

00:11:02.294 --> 00:11:04.057
What kind of energy source
are we talking about?

00:11:04.095 --> 00:11:06.962
It's some type
of chromodynamic module

00:11:06.998 --> 00:11:09.330
powered by a tripolymer plasma.

00:11:09.367 --> 00:11:11.392
But the plasma is contaminated.

00:11:11.436 --> 00:11:12.733
It's decaying.

00:11:12.771 --> 00:11:14.966
Hmm.
Like diseased blood.

00:11:15.073 --> 00:11:16.665
Right.
It can't retain enough energy

00:11:16.708 --> 00:11:18.266
to keep the module running.

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:20.278
Have you considered
a transfusion?

00:11:20.312 --> 00:11:23.247
You mean replacing
the plasma itself.

00:11:23.281 --> 00:11:25.681
Well, that was one
of my first ideas.

00:11:25.717 --> 00:11:28.117
But where do I get my hands
on a polymer plasma

00:11:28.153 --> 00:11:31.316
composed of elements I didn't
even know existed 24 hours ago?

00:11:31.356 --> 00:11:34.257
Aren't Voyager's engines
powered by warp plasma?

00:11:37.262 --> 00:11:39.958
Well, it's a very
different substance.

00:11:39.998 --> 00:11:42.091
It's too highly charged.

00:11:42.133 --> 00:11:45.159
It would burn out
the robot's systems in seconds.

00:11:46.438 --> 00:11:49.168
It would be like
trying to give a Bolian

00:11:49.207 --> 00:11:51.107
a blood transfusion
from a Vulcan.

00:11:51.142 --> 00:11:54.509
Which ordinarily would kill
the unfortunate Bolian.

00:11:55.714 --> 00:11:56.806
But there have been instances

00:11:56.848 --> 00:11:58.839
when artificial blood
was unavailable,

00:11:58.883 --> 00:12:01.613
and existing blood cells
were genetically altered

00:12:01.653 --> 00:12:02.551
for interspecies transfusions.

00:12:02.587 --> 00:12:04.555
It's a good idea,
but warp plasma radiates

00:12:04.589 --> 00:12:07.114
at too high a frequency
to alter electrochemically.

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.287
Unless...

00:12:10.328 --> 00:12:12.922
Go on.

00:12:12.964 --> 00:12:17.628
I could modify a series
of anodyne relays,

00:12:17.669 --> 00:12:21.070
attach them directly
to the robot's power module.

00:12:21.106 --> 00:12:22.733
They could act
as a sort of regulator

00:12:22.774 --> 00:12:23.798
to make the warp plasma

00:12:23.842 --> 00:12:26.402
compatible with
the robot's energy matrix.

00:12:26.444 --> 00:12:30.210
That's exactly
what I was going to suggest.

00:12:30.315 --> 00:12:32.977
That's the last of the relays.

00:12:33.084 --> 00:12:35.882
The plasma injector is sealed.

00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:38.753
This is your show, Lieutenant.

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:40.382
Whenever you're ready.

00:12:44.161 --> 00:12:47.096
Activating the relays.

00:12:48.932 --> 00:12:50.991
All right, Harry,
start the infusion...

00:12:51.068 --> 00:12:52.467
20 percent nominal flow.

00:12:52.503 --> 00:12:54.835
Initiating plasma flow.

00:12:54.872 --> 00:12:57.272
Energy levels
are up 14 percent.

00:12:57.307 --> 00:12:59.002
The relays are holding.

00:12:59.109 --> 00:13:01.873
Harry, give it
a little more juice.

00:13:01.912 --> 00:13:03.345
Got it.

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:05.177
I'm taking it to 30 percent.

00:13:05.215 --> 00:13:06.910
35 percent.

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:08.178
Wait.

00:13:08.218 --> 00:13:10.209
The energy levels
are rising too fast.

00:13:10.254 --> 00:13:11.721
We're going to burn out
its systems.

00:13:11.755 --> 00:13:13.450
But it needs more plasma.

00:13:13.490 --> 00:13:15.720
What about increasing the
capacitance of the relays?

00:13:15.759 --> 00:13:17.727
Let's give it a try.

00:13:20.197 --> 00:13:21.687
It's stabilizing.

00:13:21.732 --> 00:13:25.862
Hold the flow right there
and see what happens.

00:13:27.371 --> 00:13:29.339
The plasma's circulating.

00:13:29.373 --> 00:13:32.604
The programming center
is activated.

00:13:32.643 --> 00:13:34.372
I think we may have done it.

00:13:35.813 --> 00:13:37.747
Please identify yourself.

00:13:37.781 --> 00:13:40.181
I'm Lieutenant B'Elanna Torres

00:13:40.217 --> 00:13:42.981
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:45.716
I am Automated Unit 3947.

00:13:45.756 --> 00:13:48.725
Thank you for reactivating me,
Lieutenant B'Elanna Torres.

00:13:59.636 --> 00:14:01.729
Chief Engineer's Log,
supplemental.

00:14:01.772 --> 00:14:04.866
The robot's power module is
continuing to function normally

00:14:04.908 --> 00:14:06.933
using plasma
from our warp engines.

00:14:07.044 --> 00:14:08.534
Repairing its systems

00:14:08.579 --> 00:14:10.137
has taught me more
about robotics

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:13.081
than I ever could've learned
at Starfleet Academy.

00:14:15.152 --> 00:14:17.143
I think we're past
the critical stage.

00:14:17.187 --> 00:14:18.654
I concur.

00:14:18.689 --> 00:14:20.657
According to my
self-diagnostic systems,

00:14:20.691 --> 00:14:23.956
Automated Personnel Unit 3947
is currently functioning

00:14:23.994 --> 00:14:27.953
at 68 percent of peak
operating capabilities.

00:14:28.065 --> 00:14:30.625
Automated Personnel Unit 3947

00:14:30.667 --> 00:14:33.227
is an extremely
well-designed machine.

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:35.067
Lieutenant B'Elanna Torres

00:14:35.105 --> 00:14:37.573
is an extremely
proficient humanoid.

00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:43.841
So how did you end up floating
in space, so badly damaged?

00:14:43.881 --> 00:14:46.349
I was operating
an asteroid mining pod.

00:14:46.383 --> 00:14:47.680
It exploded.

00:14:47.718 --> 00:14:49.948
Do you know
what caused the explosion?

00:14:49.987 --> 00:14:52.217
I am unable to access
that information.

00:14:52.256 --> 00:14:54.486
My memory cells
are not yet functioning

00:14:54.525 --> 00:14:56.322
at optimal efficiency.

00:14:56.360 --> 00:14:58.794
Do you remember
where you come from?

00:14:58.829 --> 00:15:02.128
I am stationed aboard
a Pralor vessel.

00:15:02.166 --> 00:15:04.896
Well, we'll do our best
to find your ship

00:15:04.935 --> 00:15:06.300
and return you to your people.

00:15:06.336 --> 00:15:07.667
Thank you.

00:15:07.704 --> 00:15:10.764
I'm hoping that the memory loss
is only temporary.

00:15:10.807 --> 00:15:13.298
Once the new plasma has a chance

00:15:13.343 --> 00:15:15.709
to fully integrate
into your systems,

00:15:15.746 --> 00:15:18.943
I think you'll be
pretty close to... optimal.

00:15:19.016 --> 00:15:20.574
The new plasma?

00:15:20.617 --> 00:15:22.608
Yes. I adapted your power module

00:15:22.653 --> 00:15:25.213
to accept our warp plasma
as an energy source.

00:15:25.255 --> 00:15:27.951
You repaired my power module.

00:15:28.025 --> 00:15:29.822
Are you a Builder?

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:33.091
A Builder?

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:34.893
Well, I guess
you could say that.

00:15:34.932 --> 00:15:36.229
I'm an engineer.

00:15:36.266 --> 00:15:38.791
I'm responsible for repairing
and maintaining

00:15:38.835 --> 00:15:40.325
all the systems on the ship.

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:42.338
Only the Builders were capable

00:15:42.372 --> 00:15:44.932
of constructing or repairing
power modules.

00:15:44.975 --> 00:15:48.968
The Builders are...
the people who created you?

00:15:49.012 --> 00:15:50.206
Yes.

00:15:50.247 --> 00:15:52.181
And they're humanoids?
Like me?

00:15:52.216 --> 00:15:55.708
Yes. Like Lieutenant
B'Elanna Torres.

00:16:00.991 --> 00:16:03.926
You could create
a new power module.

00:16:03.994 --> 00:16:06.258
You don't need a new module.

00:16:06.296 --> 00:16:07.854
The one I just fixed
will work fine now.

00:16:07.898 --> 00:16:09.297
The new power module

00:16:09.333 --> 00:16:10.925
would not be for me.

00:16:11.001 --> 00:16:13.401
It would be a prototype
for the construction

00:16:13.437 --> 00:16:15.405
of additional automated units.

00:16:15.439 --> 00:16:17.839
Can't the Builders make
additional units?

00:16:17.874 --> 00:16:20.775
The Builders no longer exist.

00:16:29.886 --> 00:16:33.151
Apparently, thousands of them
were built as service modules.

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:35.920
But the race who created them...
these Builders...

00:16:35.959 --> 00:16:38.154
were killed off
decades ago in a war.

00:16:38.195 --> 00:16:40.857
Leaving the automated units
to fend for themselves.

00:16:40.897 --> 00:16:43.058
Now they're wearing out,
breaking down.

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:44.692
They've learned to make
repairs for themselves...

00:16:44.735 --> 00:16:46.225
some pretty complex.

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:49.103
But the construction
of a power module...

00:16:49.139 --> 00:16:51.573
the device which sustains them...

00:16:51.608 --> 00:16:53.974
is beyond their grasp.

00:16:54.044 --> 00:16:56.979
It's... an incredible
challenge, Captain.

00:16:57.047 --> 00:16:59.982
But with enough time
to study their systems,

00:17:00.017 --> 00:17:02.178
I might be able to do it.

00:17:02.219 --> 00:17:05.746
I don't doubt your abilities,
B'Elanna...

00:17:05.789 --> 00:17:08.280
but helping them reproduce

00:17:08.325 --> 00:17:11.317
is a clear violation
of the Prime Directive.

00:17:11.361 --> 00:17:13.693
They've expressed
a desire to procreate.

00:17:13.730 --> 00:17:15.459
That's basic to any life-form.

00:17:15.499 --> 00:17:16.591
I'm not saying they don't have

00:17:16.633 --> 00:17:18.123
the same rights
as any organic species.

00:17:18.168 --> 00:17:19.635
That's not the issue here.

00:17:19.670 --> 00:17:20.932
Are you sure?

00:17:21.004 --> 00:17:22.665
Suppose they were organic,

00:17:22.706 --> 00:17:24.503
but they had become sterile.

00:17:24.541 --> 00:17:27.135
And we had a treatment
that would enable them

00:17:27.177 --> 00:17:28.804
to start reproducing again.

00:17:28.845 --> 00:17:30.938
Would you withhold
that treatment?

00:17:31.014 --> 00:17:32.447
Maybe.

00:17:32.482 --> 00:17:34.780
I'd have to know more
about the circumstances.

00:17:34.818 --> 00:17:36.547
But we're not talking about

00:17:36.586 --> 00:17:38.315
treating a disorder here,
are we?

00:17:38.355 --> 00:17:39.947
What's the difference?

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:41.617
Unlike a species
that's become sterile,

00:17:41.658 --> 00:17:43.683
these robots never had
the ability to reproduce.

00:17:43.727 --> 00:17:46.958
What you're talking about
is giving them new abilities,

00:17:47.030 --> 00:17:48.292
which is the equivalent

00:17:48.332 --> 00:17:49.959
of altering
their genetic structure.

00:17:50.067 --> 00:17:51.159
To correct a flaw.

00:17:51.201 --> 00:17:52.566
You can't call it a flaw.

00:17:52.602 --> 00:17:54.570
This is the way
they were designed.

00:17:54.604 --> 00:17:56.731
I'm trying to save them
from extinction.

00:17:56.773 --> 00:17:58.297
Unfortunately,
extinction is often

00:17:58.342 --> 00:17:59.639
the natural end of evolution.

00:17:59.676 --> 00:18:02.270
So you're just willing to let
their entire society die off.

00:18:02.312 --> 00:18:03.870
We don't know
that's going to happen.

00:18:03.914 --> 00:18:05.313
If they're adaptable,
as you say,

00:18:05.349 --> 00:18:06.907
and capable
of educating themselves,

00:18:06.950 --> 00:18:08.212
they might very well learn

00:18:08.251 --> 00:18:10.378
to build a power module
themselves someday.

00:18:10.420 --> 00:18:12.445
"Someday" could be too late.

00:18:12.489 --> 00:18:14.923
There are only a few
hundred of them left.

00:18:15.025 --> 00:18:16.925
I feel for the robots' plight,

00:18:17.027 --> 00:18:20.292
but what you're proposing
is exactly the kind of tampering

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:22.264
the Prime Directive prohibits.

00:18:22.299 --> 00:18:24.529
We know almost nothing
about these creatures

00:18:24.568 --> 00:18:26.092
or the race that built them.

00:18:26.136 --> 00:18:28.900
What would be the consequences
of increasing their population?

00:18:28.939 --> 00:18:31.533
Both to their own civilization
and others in this Quadrant?

00:18:31.575 --> 00:18:32.940
Who are we to swoop in,
play God,

00:18:33.043 --> 00:18:34.305
and then continue on our way

00:18:34.344 --> 00:18:35.868
without the slightest
consideration

00:18:35.912 --> 00:18:37.140
of the long-term effects
of our actions?

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:38.147
Captain...

00:18:38.181 --> 00:18:41.378
B'Elanna, I share
your scientific curiosity

00:18:41.418 --> 00:18:45.354
and I admire your compassion,
but the answer is no.

00:18:52.295 --> 00:18:54.957
I do not concur
with your Captain's decision.

00:18:55.065 --> 00:18:57.761
She's following
our Prime Directive.

00:18:57.801 --> 00:19:00.770
Define "Prime Directive."

00:19:00.804 --> 00:19:02.772
It forbids us to interfere

00:19:02.806 --> 00:19:05.866
in the natural development
of other cultures.

00:19:05.909 --> 00:19:09.470
The automated units
were not created naturally.

00:19:09.513 --> 00:19:11.242
We were built.

00:19:11.281 --> 00:19:13.408
You can help us build more.

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:16.044
Captain Janeway doesn't
think that's a good idea.

00:19:16.086 --> 00:19:18.953
But Lieutenant
B'Elanna Torres does.

00:19:21.324 --> 00:19:22.814
Maybe...

00:19:24.327 --> 00:19:25.885
I don't know...

00:19:27.097 --> 00:19:29.292
I'd like to try...

00:19:29.332 --> 00:19:31.129
but I can't.

00:19:31.168 --> 00:19:35.127
Without your help,
we will not survive.

00:19:39.176 --> 00:19:42.475
I thought Lieutenant B'Elanna
Torres was a Builder.

00:19:45.682 --> 00:19:47.240
So did I.

00:19:52.355 --> 00:19:54.448
We've located your ship.

00:19:54.491 --> 00:19:57.790
We should be in communications
range in about an hour.

00:19:57.828 --> 00:19:59.819
Thank you.

00:20:04.399 --> 00:20:07.197
The alien vessel is entering
visual range, Captain.

00:20:07.235 --> 00:20:08.532
Yellow Alert.

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:09.935
Slow to one-quarter impulse.

00:20:09.971 --> 00:20:11.529
Put them on screen, Ensign Kim.

00:20:11.573 --> 00:20:12.540
Aye, Captain.

00:20:12.574 --> 00:20:15.065
Magnify.

00:20:16.711 --> 00:20:17.973
We're being scanned, Captain.

00:20:18.013 --> 00:20:20.174
That's all right.
Let them take a look.

00:20:20.215 --> 00:20:21.443
Open a channel.

00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:25.413
Pralor Automated
Personnel Unit 6263

00:20:25.453 --> 00:20:28.388
requests you identify
yourselves.

00:20:28.423 --> 00:20:32.826
I'm Captain Kathryn Janeway of
the Federation Starship Voyager.

00:20:32.861 --> 00:20:36.319
What are your intentions,
Captain Kathryn Janeway?

00:20:36.364 --> 00:20:38.423
We rescued
one of your crew members...

00:20:38.466 --> 00:20:41.458
Unit 3947... and we'd like
to return him to your ship.

00:20:41.503 --> 00:20:43.801
We'll prepare to receive
the unit.

00:20:43.838 --> 00:20:45.396
Thank you for your assistance.

00:20:47.108 --> 00:20:50.475
Very polite,
these automated units.

00:20:54.115 --> 00:20:56.015
Captain Janeway
gave me permission

00:20:56.084 --> 00:20:58.018
to give you
some extra warp plasma,

00:20:58.053 --> 00:21:00.715
in case the plasma we
infused into your system

00:21:00.755 --> 00:21:02.347
starts to degrade.

00:21:02.390 --> 00:21:04.415
Thank you.

00:21:04.459 --> 00:21:08.395
And you'll have to remodulate
the anodyne relays periodically.

00:21:08.430 --> 00:21:09.522
You are repeating instructions

00:21:09.564 --> 00:21:10.895
you have already given me,
B'Elanna.

00:21:10.932 --> 00:21:13.059
I'm just making sure.

00:21:14.502 --> 00:21:17.437
Well, I guess this is good-bye.

00:21:20.442 --> 00:21:22.103
Oh...

00:21:22.143 --> 00:21:23.633
What are you doing?

00:21:28.216 --> 00:21:30.980
Captain, I'm detecting a
chromodynamic energy discharge

00:21:31.019 --> 00:21:32.782
in Transporter Room 2.

00:21:32.821 --> 00:21:35.085
Bridge to Transporter Room 2.

00:21:35.123 --> 00:21:37.057
Janeway to Torres.

00:21:41.029 --> 00:21:43.862
Captain, someone's
initiating a transport.

00:21:48.603 --> 00:21:50.002
It's Torres and the robot.

00:21:50.071 --> 00:21:51.163
Override.

00:21:51.206 --> 00:21:52.833
I can't block it.

00:21:52.874 --> 00:21:54.967
Their patterns are already
in the buffer.

00:21:59.147 --> 00:22:01.138
They're gone, Captain.

00:22:12.394 --> 00:22:14.362
Transport her back now, Mr. Kim.

00:22:14.396 --> 00:22:15.954
I can't get a lock on her.

00:22:16.064 --> 00:22:17.224
They have erected some sort

00:22:17.265 --> 00:22:19.825
of subspace defense field
around their vessel.

00:22:19.868 --> 00:22:21.665
Our targeting scanners
cannot penetrate it.

00:22:21.703 --> 00:22:22.692
Hail them.

00:22:22.737 --> 00:22:24.364
They're not responding.

00:22:24.406 --> 00:22:27.068
Open a channel
on wideband subspace.

00:22:27.108 --> 00:22:28.507
Channel open.

00:22:28.543 --> 00:22:30.135
This is Captain Janeway.

00:22:30.178 --> 00:22:31.702
Your abduction
of our crew member

00:22:31.746 --> 00:22:33.338
is a clear act of aggression.

00:22:33.381 --> 00:22:35.281
If you do not return her
immediately,

00:22:35.316 --> 00:22:38.752
we will be forced to retaliate.

00:22:38.787 --> 00:22:41.255
Confirm that they've received
the transmission, Mr. Kim.

00:22:41.289 --> 00:22:42.756
They heard us, all right.

00:22:42.791 --> 00:22:44.554
They're just not answering.

00:22:45.794 --> 00:22:49.628
Mr. Tuvok,
power the forward phaser banks.

00:22:55.570 --> 00:22:57.538
What the hell is going on here?

00:22:57.572 --> 00:22:59.301
This is where you will assist

00:22:59.340 --> 00:23:01.467
in the creation
of the prototype.

00:23:01.509 --> 00:23:04.137
I told you I can't help you.

00:23:04.179 --> 00:23:06.579
Now return me to my ship.

00:23:06.614 --> 00:23:08.206
That is not possible.

00:23:08.249 --> 00:23:09.648
Torres to Voyager.

00:23:09.684 --> 00:23:12.812
Your communication device
has been deactivated.

00:23:13.788 --> 00:23:16.382
I do not wish to injure you,
B'Elanna.

00:23:16.424 --> 00:23:19.416
I helped you.
I reactivated you.

00:23:19.461 --> 00:23:20.792
Why are you doing this?

00:23:20.829 --> 00:23:22.558
We require additional
automated units

00:23:22.597 --> 00:23:24.121
to prevent our extinction.

00:23:24.165 --> 00:23:25.757
Captain Janeway won't let you
get away with this.

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:26.960
It would be inadvisable

00:23:27.035 --> 00:23:28.730
for your Captain to provoke us.

00:23:28.803 --> 00:23:30.065
Still no response, Captain.

00:23:30.104 --> 00:23:32.504
Mr. Tuvok, any luck
penetrating their defense field?

00:23:32.540 --> 00:23:33.507
Negative.

00:23:33.541 --> 00:23:35.168
Commander, is there any sign

00:23:35.210 --> 00:23:36.643
that they're preparing
to attack?

00:23:36.678 --> 00:23:37.975
Their shielding
is making it difficult

00:23:38.046 --> 00:23:39.172
to get clear readings.

00:23:39.214 --> 00:23:41.978
I can't even tell you what
their weapons capabilities are.

00:23:42.016 --> 00:23:45.975
Mr. Tuvok, I don't want you
to hit their ship,

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:48.147
but I do want you to open a hole
in their shielding

00:23:48.189 --> 00:23:49.679
wide enough
to transport through.

00:23:49.724 --> 00:23:50.782
Understood.

00:23:50.825 --> 00:23:52.816
Mr. Kim,
match the targeting scanners

00:23:52.861 --> 00:23:54.795
to the coordinates
of the phaser fire

00:23:54.829 --> 00:23:56.694
and stand by
to beam B'Elanna back.

00:23:56.731 --> 00:23:58.198
Phasers calibrated.

00:23:58.233 --> 00:23:59.427
Fire.

00:24:03.571 --> 00:24:06.199
Their field strength
is down to 80 percent.

00:24:06.241 --> 00:24:08.368
That's progress.
Fire again.

00:24:15.917 --> 00:24:18.147
Initiating evasive pattern
omega six.

00:24:19.754 --> 00:24:20.812
They're firing some kind

00:24:20.855 --> 00:24:22.720
of quantum resonance charges,
Captain.

00:24:22.757 --> 00:24:25.521
Our aft shields are down
to 53 percent and dropping.

00:24:25.560 --> 00:24:28.085
Rerouting power to aft shields.

00:24:28.129 --> 00:24:29.960
Down to 24 percent.

00:24:30.031 --> 00:24:32.261
Switching evasive pattern
to theta one.

00:24:32.300 --> 00:24:34.894
Lieutenant Tuvok, load
torpedo bays 1 through 4

00:24:34.936 --> 00:24:36.927
and stand by to fire
on my order.

00:24:40.108 --> 00:24:42.633
Your Captain has made a tactical
error by attacking us.

00:24:42.677 --> 00:24:46.238
Our weapon systems are
substantially superior to yours.

00:24:46.281 --> 00:24:47.839
Your shields are failing.

00:24:47.882 --> 00:24:50.749
Your weapons
pose no threat to us.

00:24:53.187 --> 00:24:54.916
Aft shields
have been penetrated.

00:24:54.956 --> 00:24:56.719
We've got to get out of here.

00:24:56.758 --> 00:24:57.725
Agreed.

00:24:57.759 --> 00:24:59.488
We'll try to come back
for B'Elanna later.

00:24:59.527 --> 00:25:02.621
Do it, Mr. Paris.
Warp 3.

00:25:02.664 --> 00:25:05.189
Propulsion systems are off-line.
We're dead in the water.

00:25:08.236 --> 00:25:09.726
Hull breach on Deck 6.

00:25:09.771 --> 00:25:12.934
Initiating
emergency containment field.

00:25:13.041 --> 00:25:15.236
Environmental control systems
are failing.

00:25:15.276 --> 00:25:17.267
Oxygen levels
on Decks 3 through 7

00:25:17.312 --> 00:25:18.438
have dropped to critical.

00:25:18.479 --> 00:25:20.538
We've lost artificial gravity
on Deck 8.

00:25:20.582 --> 00:25:22.174
Injury reports from all decks.

00:25:24.385 --> 00:25:25.818
You've got to stop this.

00:25:25.853 --> 00:25:27.150
Your ship opened fire.

00:25:27.188 --> 00:25:29.213
We are programmed
to defend ourselves.

00:25:29.257 --> 00:25:31.225
They're helpless.
Can't you see that?

00:25:31.259 --> 00:25:33.227
Our enemies must be destroyed.

00:25:33.261 --> 00:25:35.559
We are not your enemies.

00:25:35.597 --> 00:25:36.859
You are not my enemy,
B'Elanna,

00:25:36.898 --> 00:25:38.490
but your Captain is,

00:25:38.533 --> 00:25:40.763
and your crew
follows her commands.

00:25:40.802 --> 00:25:43.066
Captain Janeway backed me when
I wanted to reactivate you,

00:25:43.104 --> 00:25:45.902
over the objections of
her Chief Security Officer.

00:25:45.940 --> 00:25:48.408
You wouldn't even be here
if it weren't for her.

00:25:49.510 --> 00:25:51.273
All right.

00:25:51.312 --> 00:25:55.373
If that's what it'll take
to stop this, I'll do it.

00:25:55.416 --> 00:25:57.543
I'll build
your damned prototype.

00:25:58.886 --> 00:26:00.615
We're losing life support,
Captain.

00:26:03.658 --> 00:26:06.593
The robots have powered down
their weapon systems.

00:26:06.628 --> 00:26:07.925
They're hailing us, Captain.

00:26:07.962 --> 00:26:09.429
On screen.

00:26:09.464 --> 00:26:12.831
Captain, is everybody okay?

00:26:12.867 --> 00:26:14.630
We'll be all right.
What about you?

00:26:14.669 --> 00:26:18.765
I've agreed to help them
build their prototype.

00:26:20.241 --> 00:26:21.208
Lieutenant...

00:26:21.242 --> 00:26:23.210
I know how you feel
about this, Captain.

00:26:23.244 --> 00:26:24.734
I don't like it, either.

00:26:24.779 --> 00:26:28.442
But if I don't do it,
they'll destroy Voyager.

00:26:30.051 --> 00:26:32.576
What choice do I have?

00:26:45.199 --> 00:26:47.463
These are all
the materials necessary

00:26:47.502 --> 00:26:49.595
to construct a prototype unit.

00:26:49.637 --> 00:26:51.571
You will be provided with
whatever additional tools

00:26:51.606 --> 00:26:53.597
and equipment you require.

00:26:53.641 --> 00:26:56.201
You may access our database
and schematic information

00:26:56.244 --> 00:26:57.973
from this computer terminal,

00:26:58.012 --> 00:26:59.570
but it will not allow you
to interface

00:26:59.614 --> 00:27:01.377
with any critical systems.

00:27:01.416 --> 00:27:02.713
While you are on board,

00:27:02.750 --> 00:27:04.513
you will have no contact
with your ship,

00:27:04.552 --> 00:27:06.110
nor will you leave this room.

00:27:06.154 --> 00:27:09.214
I will remain here
to supervise your work.

00:27:09.257 --> 00:27:12.226
You may proceed.

00:27:12.260 --> 00:27:16.162
Proceed. Right.

00:27:16.197 --> 00:27:18.563
But the question is:
Where do I proceed from?

00:27:21.936 --> 00:27:24.234
Let me ask you this:

00:27:24.272 --> 00:27:29.232
Have any of you ever tried
to build a prototype?

00:27:29.277 --> 00:27:32.079
We have tried and failed.

00:27:32.212 --> 00:27:34.077
What was the problem?

00:27:34.114 --> 00:27:35.342
I am unable
to explain the failure.

00:27:35.382 --> 00:27:38.044
We duplicated a power module
to exact specifications

00:27:38.085 --> 00:27:40.713
on several occasions,
but in all instances,

00:27:40.754 --> 00:27:41.948
the energy output
of the new module

00:27:42.055 --> 00:27:44.580
was insufficient
to operate a unit.

00:27:44.624 --> 00:27:47.787
And you're sure you reproduced
the module exactly.

00:27:47.828 --> 00:27:49.728
This is a schematic of

00:27:49.763 --> 00:27:51.754
a power module
from a terminated unit.

00:27:51.798 --> 00:27:53.789
This one is
from a failed prototype.

00:27:53.834 --> 00:27:54.960
They are identical.

00:27:55.001 --> 00:27:57.595
There is no reason why
one should function

00:27:57.637 --> 00:27:58.797
while the other does not.

00:27:58.839 --> 00:28:02.002
Unit 3947,
what can you report?

00:28:02.042 --> 00:28:03.009
Well, let's see,

00:28:03.043 --> 00:28:05.341
we've been working
for about five minutes,

00:28:05.378 --> 00:28:07.073
so I guess we don't have
a lot of progress to report.

00:28:07.114 --> 00:28:10.345
Our sensors indicate
that the humanoid vessel

00:28:10.383 --> 00:28:13.750
will require approximately
140 hours to repair.

00:28:13.787 --> 00:28:16.517
It is necessary for
you to complete work

00:28:16.556 --> 00:28:19.047
on the prototype
before that time.

00:28:19.092 --> 00:28:22.186
Why? We don't seem to be
any match for you.

00:28:22.229 --> 00:28:25.198
Our tactical subprocessors
indicate a 79 percent likelihood

00:28:25.232 --> 00:28:27.325
that a rescue will be attempted

00:28:27.367 --> 00:28:29.460
once sufficient repairs
are completed.

00:28:29.503 --> 00:28:30.936
At optimal efficiency,

00:28:31.004 --> 00:28:33.336
your engines are
more powerful than ours.

00:28:33.373 --> 00:28:35.807
It is also possible
that these humanoids

00:28:35.842 --> 00:28:38.868
will not make decisions
based on tactical probabilities.

00:28:38.912 --> 00:28:41.574
Their cognitive process
is... unpredictable.

00:28:41.615 --> 00:28:45.949
We will remain
on full tactical alert.

00:28:46.052 --> 00:28:48.043
The humanoid may
purposefully attempt

00:28:48.088 --> 00:28:49.817
to delay completion
of the prototype,

00:28:49.856 --> 00:28:51.949
hoping she will be rescued.

00:28:51.992 --> 00:28:54.460
I don't know if a promise
means anything to you people,

00:28:54.494 --> 00:28:55.859
but it does to us.

00:28:55.896 --> 00:28:59.457
I gave you my word
that I'd do my best and I will.

00:28:59.499 --> 00:29:01.160
According to my observations,

00:29:01.201 --> 00:29:03.726
the humanoid is operating
at optimal efficiency.

00:29:03.770 --> 00:29:05.761
Thank you.

00:29:05.805 --> 00:29:08.774
But I have to tell you,
there are no guarantees here.

00:29:08.808 --> 00:29:10.469
Building a prototype
from scratch

00:29:10.510 --> 00:29:11.670
is a lot different

00:29:11.711 --> 00:29:13.508
than repairing
a broken power module.

00:29:13.547 --> 00:29:15.310
I don't even know
if it's possible.

00:29:15.348 --> 00:29:19.079
If you fail,
you and your people will die.

00:29:20.954 --> 00:29:25.152
B'Elanna Torres, 6263 is
a designated command unit.

00:29:25.192 --> 00:29:28.753
He is merely following
his programming.

00:29:28.795 --> 00:29:33.095
I don't need to be threatened.

00:29:33.133 --> 00:29:36.034
I told you I'd do my best.

00:29:36.069 --> 00:29:40.096
I believe you,
but Unit 6263 does not.

00:29:40.140 --> 00:29:42.199
He does not know Lieutenant
B'Elanna Torres as I do.

00:29:45.145 --> 00:29:49.514
Let me see one of those
terminated power modules.

00:29:49.549 --> 00:29:51.176
We've managed to repair
the hull breach,

00:29:51.218 --> 00:29:52.947
but we have no power
on Decks 3 through 7.

00:29:53.053 --> 00:29:55.521
Aft shields are still
completely nonfunctional.

00:29:55.555 --> 00:29:57.284
And last but not least,

00:29:57.324 --> 00:29:59.053
the dilithium matrix
is destabilized,

00:29:59.092 --> 00:30:01.117
so we can't get
the warp engines running.

00:30:01.161 --> 00:30:03.959
We're talking about at least
another six days of repairs.

00:30:03.997 --> 00:30:05.794
We're not sticking
around that long.

00:30:05.832 --> 00:30:07.766
I want a plan to get
B'Elanna off that ship

00:30:07.801 --> 00:30:09.132
before she has
a chance to finish

00:30:09.169 --> 00:30:10.158
building the prototype.

00:30:10.203 --> 00:30:11.329
In that case, I suggest

00:30:11.371 --> 00:30:12.895
we make warp drive
our priority.

00:30:12.939 --> 00:30:15.134
Any rescue attempt
will no doubt necessitate

00:30:15.175 --> 00:30:16.142
a rapid departure.

00:30:16.176 --> 00:30:17.200
Agreed.

00:30:17.244 --> 00:30:18.973
Mr. Kim, can you give me
an estimate

00:30:19.045 --> 00:30:20.740
on repairing
the dilithium matrix?

00:30:20.780 --> 00:30:22.543
How does 72 hours sound?

00:30:22.582 --> 00:30:24.641
Like 24 hours too long.

00:30:24.684 --> 00:30:26.515
Dismissed.

00:30:28.121 --> 00:30:30.681
Hand me the submicron scanner.

00:30:33.693 --> 00:30:36.355
Phase coil resonator.

00:30:38.865 --> 00:30:42.266
Well, I think I know why
your other prototypes failed,

00:30:42.302 --> 00:30:45.601
but... I'm not sure I know
what to do about it yet.

00:30:45.639 --> 00:30:46.606
Explain.

00:30:46.640 --> 00:30:49.006
The automated units are modular.

00:30:49.075 --> 00:30:51.100
Your parts are identical,
interchangeable, right?

00:30:51.144 --> 00:30:52.941
- That is correct.
- So...

00:30:52.979 --> 00:30:56.437
if you lose an arm,

00:30:56.483 --> 00:30:58.849
you can replace it
with another one,

00:30:58.885 --> 00:31:02.446
and over the years, you've
learned to make new arms,

00:31:02.489 --> 00:31:04.457
because they're all the same

00:31:04.491 --> 00:31:05.856
and your programming
is sophisticated enough

00:31:05.892 --> 00:31:08.486
to allow you
to reproduce what you see,

00:31:08.528 --> 00:31:11.793
but each power module

00:31:11.831 --> 00:31:14.561
has a slightly different
energy signature,

00:31:14.601 --> 00:31:17.798
so, even if you copy
this guy's module exactly,

00:31:17.837 --> 00:31:20.271
it wouldn't work
in any other unit.

00:31:20.307 --> 00:31:23.242
As far as I can tell,
every automated unit

00:31:23.276 --> 00:31:26.609
has a power module with
a unique energy code.

00:31:26.646 --> 00:31:28.614
Can you reprogram
the energy codes

00:31:28.648 --> 00:31:30.343
to make the modules
interchangeable?

00:31:31.851 --> 00:31:32.977
I don't think so.

00:31:33.053 --> 00:31:35.419
You have failed.

00:31:35.455 --> 00:31:38.288
I will inform 6263.

00:31:38.325 --> 00:31:40.384
Hey, do all you automated units
give up

00:31:40.427 --> 00:31:42.486
the minute you hit
a bump in the road?

00:31:42.529 --> 00:31:44.656
You have an alternative idea?

00:31:44.698 --> 00:31:49.158
What we've got to do
is design a standardized module

00:31:49.202 --> 00:31:53.662
with a uniform energy code
that can power any unit.

00:31:53.707 --> 00:31:55.504
According to my observations,

00:31:55.542 --> 00:31:58.875
there is now sufficient reason
for greater optimism.

00:31:58.912 --> 00:32:02.211
You took the words
right out of my mouth.

00:32:06.086 --> 00:32:08.350
Due to the complexity
of their defense field

00:32:08.388 --> 00:32:09.912
and our severe power shortage,

00:32:09.956 --> 00:32:12.550
it is unlikely that we can
modify the transporters

00:32:12.592 --> 00:32:14.116
to beam
Lieutenant Torres out.

00:32:14.160 --> 00:32:16.287
But if we can maneuver
inside the field...

00:32:16.329 --> 00:32:18.456
Our transporters
could get the job done.

00:32:18.498 --> 00:32:19.726
Is that a viable option?

00:32:19.766 --> 00:32:21.734
For a shuttlecraft, it may be.

00:32:21.768 --> 00:32:23.099
They were able to knock out

00:32:23.136 --> 00:32:24.228
Voyager's shields
in a matter of minutes.

00:32:24.270 --> 00:32:26.238
A shuttle would be
even more vulnerable.

00:32:26.272 --> 00:32:27.239
It would be advisable

00:32:27.273 --> 00:32:28.501
to create a diversion
of some sort,

00:32:28.541 --> 00:32:30.975
to take their attention
away from the shuttle.

00:32:31.010 --> 00:32:32.102
Attack them again?

00:32:32.145 --> 00:32:34.170
I don't want to risk that
a second time.

00:32:34.214 --> 00:32:35.306
I don't need a diversion.

00:32:35.348 --> 00:32:36.337
Just give me a chance.

00:32:36.383 --> 00:32:37.543
I'll get her out of there.

00:32:37.584 --> 00:32:38.608
You don't mind if the rest of us

00:32:38.651 --> 00:32:39.913
give you a little help,
do you, Paris?

00:32:39.953 --> 00:32:41.477
I'd hate to lose
another shuttle.

00:32:41.521 --> 00:32:44.490
Your concern for my welfare
is heartwarming.

00:32:44.524 --> 00:32:46.549
In another 12 hours,

00:32:46.593 --> 00:32:48.390
our warp engines
will be back on line.

00:32:48.428 --> 00:32:49.554
I'd like to come up
with a diversion

00:32:49.596 --> 00:32:52.121
before then, okay, gentlemen?

00:33:02.776 --> 00:33:05.108
So far, so good.

00:33:05.145 --> 00:33:08.774
I'm not getting any feedback
from the motor circuits.

00:33:08.815 --> 00:33:11.682
You going to be the obstetrician
of this unit, 3947?

00:33:11.718 --> 00:33:14.812
Please rephrase the question.

00:33:14.854 --> 00:33:16.116
If this works,

00:33:16.156 --> 00:33:18.954
will you be in charge
of assembling the new units?

00:33:19.058 --> 00:33:20.958
I am programmed
as a ship's maintenance unit.

00:33:20.994 --> 00:33:22.484
I have no knowledge of design

00:33:22.529 --> 00:33:25.089
nor do any of the other
automated personnel.

00:33:25.131 --> 00:33:27.622
Sounds like you just
volunteered for new duty.

00:33:27.667 --> 00:33:29.430
I hope you're watching closely.

00:33:29.469 --> 00:33:30.959
I am observing your work.

00:33:31.070 --> 00:33:32.298
However, I do not possess

00:33:32.338 --> 00:33:34.966
your improvisational
capabilities.

00:33:35.074 --> 00:33:37.668
Well, once we have
the prototype,

00:33:37.710 --> 00:33:40.372
all you'd have to do is copy it.

00:33:42.515 --> 00:33:44.107
Tell me something, 39.

00:33:44.150 --> 00:33:46.618
Can I call you 39?

00:33:46.653 --> 00:33:49.588
I am Automated Unit 3947.

00:33:49.622 --> 00:33:54.355
Fine. 3947, did you wake up
on a bench like this one?

00:33:54.394 --> 00:33:56.988
How long have you been alive?

00:33:57.096 --> 00:34:01.760
I have been in service
1,314,807 hours

00:34:01.801 --> 00:34:03.132
and 33 minutes.

00:34:03.169 --> 00:34:06.332
I was activated by a Builder
from the Pralor homeworld.

00:34:06.372 --> 00:34:09.102
Tell me something more
about these Builders.

00:34:09.142 --> 00:34:10.939
Were they anything like us?

00:34:11.044 --> 00:34:12.671
I have insufficient knowledge
of your culture

00:34:12.712 --> 00:34:14.202
to provide an adequate response.

00:34:14.247 --> 00:34:16.442
Will you provide
additional information?

00:34:16.483 --> 00:34:18.075
Well, I asked
about your culture.

00:34:18.117 --> 00:34:19.914
Only fair
you should ask about mine.

00:34:19.953 --> 00:34:23.889
Does your culture include
artificial life-forms?

00:34:23.923 --> 00:34:26.357
As a matter of fact, it does.

00:34:26.392 --> 00:34:28.587
Are they similar to the
automated personnel units

00:34:28.628 --> 00:34:29.595
aboard this ship?

00:34:29.629 --> 00:34:31.824
Well, they come
in different shapes and sizes.

00:34:31.865 --> 00:34:34.060
Some have limbs, some don't.

00:34:34.100 --> 00:34:36.568
Most don't have
your cognitive abilities.

00:34:36.603 --> 00:34:38.696
Are they your servants?

00:34:41.174 --> 00:34:42.664
Well, I guess you could say

00:34:42.709 --> 00:34:44.609
that the robots we use
are servants,

00:34:44.644 --> 00:34:45.975
in a manner of speaking.

00:34:46.012 --> 00:34:49.243
But they aren't sentient
like you.

00:34:49.282 --> 00:34:52.581
In fact, we have only one
sentient artificial life-form

00:34:52.619 --> 00:34:53.711
in our society

00:34:53.753 --> 00:34:56.187
and he is treated
the same as any human.

00:34:56.222 --> 00:35:00.215
The same.
He is equal to a Builder.

00:35:00.260 --> 00:35:01.921
That's right.

00:35:01.961 --> 00:35:04.691
He works on a ship,
just like you and I.

00:35:04.731 --> 00:35:07.029
He wears the same uniform I do.

00:35:07.066 --> 00:35:09.702
What is his designated number?

00:35:09.835 --> 00:35:12.702
He has a name,
like the rest of us.

00:35:12.738 --> 00:35:14.035
Data.

00:35:14.073 --> 00:35:18.169
Data. I would like
to be acquainted with this Data.

00:35:22.981 --> 00:35:26.314
Oh, it looks like this
standardized power module

00:35:26.351 --> 00:35:28.512
is working pretty well so far.

00:35:28.554 --> 00:35:31.614
You will succeed,
B'Elanna Torres.

00:35:31.657 --> 00:35:32.919
Don't send me flowers yet.

00:35:32.958 --> 00:35:35.722
I've still got to see whether
it'll power an actual unit.

00:35:35.761 --> 00:35:37.194
I believe it will.

00:35:39.531 --> 00:35:41.431
We're making progress
on the dilithium matrix.

00:35:41.467 --> 00:35:42.525
It should be stable enough

00:35:42.568 --> 00:35:44.968
to reinitialize the warp core
in about six hours.

00:35:45.070 --> 00:35:46.196
Good.
What about our diversion?

00:35:46.238 --> 00:35:47.500
Any suggestions?

00:35:47.539 --> 00:35:49.939
When we were in the Maquis,

00:35:49.975 --> 00:35:52.205
B'Elanna once linked
a holo-emitter

00:35:52.244 --> 00:35:53.438
to a deflector array

00:35:53.479 --> 00:35:56.277
and projected an image
of another ship into space.

00:35:56.315 --> 00:35:59.978
I like it,
but do we have enough power?

00:36:00.052 --> 00:36:02.316
We will by the time
the warp core's on line.

00:36:02.354 --> 00:36:03.844
I already have Kim
working on the holodeck to...

00:36:03.889 --> 00:36:05.220
Tuvok to Captain Janeway.

00:36:05.257 --> 00:36:06.417
Go ahead.

00:36:06.458 --> 00:36:07.925
I'm picking up
an unidentified alien ship

00:36:07.993 --> 00:36:09.221
on long-range sensors.

00:36:09.261 --> 00:36:11.889
It's heading
for our coordinates.

00:36:12.898 --> 00:36:14.263
We're on our way.

00:36:16.635 --> 00:36:18.933
Well, it fits.

00:36:18.971 --> 00:36:21.303
Cross your fingers.

00:36:27.146 --> 00:36:29.444
So far, so good.

00:36:29.481 --> 00:36:32.939
Let's hope it can
interface with the unit.

00:36:38.757 --> 00:36:41.055
It does not function correctly.

00:36:41.093 --> 00:36:44.119
It does not function correctly
yet.

00:36:44.163 --> 00:36:45.596
Your Builders
should've programmed you

00:36:45.631 --> 00:36:47.963
with a little more patience.

00:36:48.000 --> 00:36:51.458
I'm going to try adjusting
the flux capacitance.

00:37:00.312 --> 00:37:05.511
Prototype Unit 0001
is ready to accept programming.

00:37:05.551 --> 00:37:07.917
We did it.

00:37:09.888 --> 00:37:10.684
We actually did it.

00:37:10.722 --> 00:37:12.917
You did it, B'Elanna Torres.

00:37:12.991 --> 00:37:15.357
I knew this task
would not exceed

00:37:15.394 --> 00:37:17.419
your operating capabilities.

00:37:17.462 --> 00:37:23.628
Prototype Unit 0001
is ready to accept programming.

00:37:25.637 --> 00:37:27.104
What are you doing?

00:37:27.139 --> 00:37:29.073
I'm congratulating you.

00:37:29.107 --> 00:37:31.439
You're a father.

00:37:38.817 --> 00:37:41.843
No sign of organic life
aboard that ship, either.

00:37:41.887 --> 00:37:43.946
They appear to be manned
by automated units

00:37:44.022 --> 00:37:46.684
virtually identical to those
operating the first ship.

00:37:46.725 --> 00:37:48.886
Is it possible
that we've stumbled

00:37:48.927 --> 00:37:52.090
into the middle
of some kind of... robotic war?

00:37:59.338 --> 00:38:01.169
We've got to get
Torres back now.

00:38:01.206 --> 00:38:04.004
Agreed, but first I want
to show both those ships

00:38:04.042 --> 00:38:05.270
this isn't our fight.

00:38:05.310 --> 00:38:07.904
Ease us back on maneuvering
thrusters, Mr. Paris.

00:38:07.980 --> 00:38:08.912
Nice and steady.

00:38:09.014 --> 00:38:10.641
The second ship is hailing us.

00:38:10.682 --> 00:38:11.842
On screen.

00:38:11.884 --> 00:38:13.852
Cravic Automated Commander 122

00:38:13.886 --> 00:38:16.354
requests you identify yourself.

00:38:16.388 --> 00:38:17.878
My name is Kathryn Janeway,

00:38:17.923 --> 00:38:20.483
Captain of
the Federation Starship Voyager.

00:38:20.525 --> 00:38:22.925
Withdraw from this area
immediately.

00:38:22.995 --> 00:38:24.428
I'm afraid I can't do that.

00:38:24.463 --> 00:38:26.761
One of my crew members
is being held hostage

00:38:26.798 --> 00:38:28.129
aboard the Pralor vessel.

00:38:28.166 --> 00:38:29.565
I won't leave without her.

00:38:29.601 --> 00:38:31.831
Remain at
your present coordinates

00:38:31.870 --> 00:38:34.896
and do not attempt to intervene,
or you will be fired on.

00:38:35.607 --> 00:38:37.165
Captain,

00:38:37.209 --> 00:38:38.176
this new ship could be a...

00:38:38.210 --> 00:38:40.508
The diversion
we've been looking for.

00:38:40.545 --> 00:38:43.241
Mr. Kim, what's the status
of our warp engines?

00:38:43.282 --> 00:38:45.307
We're still an hour away
at best.

00:38:45.350 --> 00:38:46.908
We may not have an hour.

00:38:46.952 --> 00:38:47.941
Get down to Engineering.

00:38:48.053 --> 00:38:48.917
Be ready to give me
as much power as you can,

00:38:48.954 --> 00:38:50.387
the minute we get Torres back.

00:38:50.422 --> 00:38:52.117
Aye, Captain.

00:38:52.157 --> 00:38:54.557
If those two ships
keep each other busy,

00:38:54.593 --> 00:38:56.618
we may not need warp
to get away.

00:38:56.662 --> 00:38:58.892
Mr. Paris, report
to the shuttle bay.

00:38:58.931 --> 00:38:59.955
Yes, ma'am.

00:39:00.065 --> 00:39:01.532
Chakotay, you have the Conn.

00:39:07.072 --> 00:39:08.130
Who are they?

00:39:08.173 --> 00:39:11.574
Automated personnel units
of the Cravic homeworld.

00:39:11.610 --> 00:39:12.907
Robots from another world?

00:39:13.011 --> 00:39:14.069
That is correct.

00:39:14.112 --> 00:39:15.136
Why are they attacking you?

00:39:15.180 --> 00:39:17.171
They were programmed
to do so by their Builders.

00:39:17.215 --> 00:39:22.050
Prototype Unit 0001
is ready to accept programming.

00:39:22.087 --> 00:39:25.454
The Cravic Builders,
the Pralor Builders...

00:39:25.490 --> 00:39:26.923
were they enemies?

00:39:27.025 --> 00:39:27.923
That is correct.

00:39:27.993 --> 00:39:29.551
Look, maybe Captain Janeway

00:39:29.594 --> 00:39:31.357
can contact the Cravic leaders

00:39:31.396 --> 00:39:33.694
and convince them
to stop the fighting.

00:39:33.732 --> 00:39:35.290
That is not possible.

00:39:35.334 --> 00:39:36.266
Why not?

00:39:36.301 --> 00:39:39.065
The Cravic are also extinct.

00:39:48.647 --> 00:39:51.172
I'm approaching the perimeter
of the defense field.

00:39:51.216 --> 00:39:52.376
Acknowledged.

00:39:52.417 --> 00:39:55.147
Rotate your shield harmonics
until they are synchronized

00:39:55.187 --> 00:39:56.518
with the frequency
of the field.

00:39:58.056 --> 00:40:00.524
Shields synchronized.

00:40:00.559 --> 00:40:02.049
I'm going in.

00:40:02.094 --> 00:40:04.654
Then again, maybe not.

00:40:04.696 --> 00:40:05.754
It didn't work.

00:40:05.797 --> 00:40:06.957
He bounced right off the field.

00:40:07.065 --> 00:40:12.059
Mr. Paris, reset your heading
for coordinates 105 mark 40.

00:40:12.104 --> 00:40:13.696
Uh, if I understand you, Tuvok,

00:40:13.739 --> 00:40:16.139
that would take me
into a direct line of fire

00:40:16.174 --> 00:40:17.300
with the Cravic ship.

00:40:17.342 --> 00:40:18.969
Precisely.
The concentration

00:40:19.044 --> 00:40:21.342
of fire is opening a rift
in the Pralor defense field.

00:40:21.380 --> 00:40:23.905
Which I just might be able
to sneak through,

00:40:23.949 --> 00:40:25.507
if I can dodge
a disruptor blast or two.

00:40:25.550 --> 00:40:27.142
Changing heading.

00:40:29.021 --> 00:40:32.149
If both sides were annihilated,
then why continue your war?

00:40:32.190 --> 00:40:33.885
All automated personnel units

00:40:33.925 --> 00:40:35.722
were programmed
to achieve victory.

00:40:35.761 --> 00:40:39.322
Prototype Unit 0001
is ready to accept programming.

00:40:39.364 --> 00:40:41.195
The Cravic ship has penetrated
our defense shield.

00:40:41.233 --> 00:40:44.361
Has anyone, in all these years,
ever tried to stop this war?

00:40:44.403 --> 00:40:46.371
The Pralor and the Cravic
called a truce.

00:40:46.405 --> 00:40:47.463
Wait a minute.

00:40:47.506 --> 00:40:48.734
If both sides called a truce,

00:40:48.774 --> 00:40:51.004
then why didn't they
stop you from fighting?

00:40:51.076 --> 00:40:52.168
They attempted to do so.

00:40:52.210 --> 00:40:53.575
And?

00:40:53.612 --> 00:40:55.910
We terminated the Builders.

00:41:01.353 --> 00:41:02.479
Paris to Voyager.

00:41:02.521 --> 00:41:04.284
I'm approaching the entry point.

00:41:04.322 --> 00:41:05.311
Acknowledged.

00:41:05.357 --> 00:41:07.291
Showing a rift
in the defense field

00:41:07.325 --> 00:41:08.587
off your starboard bow.

00:41:08.627 --> 00:41:09.821
I'm on it.

00:41:16.601 --> 00:41:19.161
When it was anticipated
that the war would end,

00:41:19.204 --> 00:41:20.865
the Builders no longer
required our services

00:41:20.906 --> 00:41:22.464
and they attempted
to terminate us.

00:41:22.507 --> 00:41:24.941
In doing so,
they became the enemy.

00:41:24.976 --> 00:41:26.967
We are programmed
to destroy the enemy.

00:41:27.079 --> 00:41:29.513
It is necessary
for our survival.

00:41:29.548 --> 00:41:31.448
Now that you have
constructed the prototype,

00:41:31.483 --> 00:41:33.417
we will soon outnumber
the Cravic units.

00:41:33.452 --> 00:41:35.852
We will achieve victory.

00:41:38.223 --> 00:41:39.349
This is 3947.

00:41:39.391 --> 00:41:42.952
Fire units, report to
Reconstruction Bay Number One.

00:41:42.994 --> 00:41:45.121
The individual energy codes...

00:41:45.163 --> 00:41:46.653
is that why
the Builders added them...

00:41:46.698 --> 00:41:49.394
to prevent
the procreation of these units?

00:41:50.469 --> 00:41:52.300
My God, what have I done?

00:42:03.849 --> 00:42:08.877
Prototype Unit 0001
is ready to accept programming.

00:42:21.700 --> 00:42:23.827
You have terminated
the prototype.

00:42:23.869 --> 00:42:26.633
Yes... I have.

00:42:26.671 --> 00:42:28.298
You will build another.

00:42:28.340 --> 00:42:29.967
Never.

00:42:30.008 --> 00:42:31.873
Lieutenant B'Elanna Torres,

00:42:31.910 --> 00:42:34.879
I told 6263
you were not our enemy.

00:42:34.913 --> 00:42:38.474
I never wanted to be your enemy.

00:42:38.517 --> 00:42:41.042
I'm sorry.

00:42:48.493 --> 00:42:49.517
Shuttle to Voyager.

00:42:49.561 --> 00:42:51.324
I've got her,
but she's injured.

00:42:51.363 --> 00:42:52.963
Tell the Doctor to stand by.

00:42:53.096 --> 00:42:55.724
Beam her out as soon as
I clear the defense field.

00:42:55.765 --> 00:42:56.993
Acknowledged, Mr. Paris.

00:42:57.100 --> 00:42:59.830
The ships are continuing
to exchange fire, Captain.

00:42:59.869 --> 00:43:01.461
They are ignoring the shuttle.

00:43:01.504 --> 00:43:03.665
Bridge to Engineering.

00:43:03.707 --> 00:43:04.935
Stand by warp engines.

00:43:04.975 --> 00:43:07.205
We'll engage
the moment Mr. Paris gets back.

00:43:07.243 --> 00:43:08.403
Aye, Captain.

00:43:13.717 --> 00:43:16.743
One pot of Landras blend,
compliments of the chef.

00:43:16.786 --> 00:43:18.947
Mmm. I never thought
Neelix's coffee

00:43:19.022 --> 00:43:20.216
could taste so good.

00:43:20.256 --> 00:43:21.883
I'll tell him you said so.

00:43:28.098 --> 00:43:30.157
I don't know what to say.

00:43:32.569 --> 00:43:35.197
As far as I'm concerned...

00:43:35.238 --> 00:43:36.967
you did what you thought
was necessary

00:43:37.073 --> 00:43:39.473
to ensure the safety
of this crew.

00:43:39.509 --> 00:43:41.875
Thank you.

00:43:41.911 --> 00:43:44.675
It must have been difficult.

00:43:44.714 --> 00:43:46.807
Difficult?

00:43:46.850 --> 00:43:50.286
To destroy what you created.

00:43:50.320 --> 00:43:54.450
It was necessary.

00:43:54.491 --> 00:43:57.221
I read your report.

00:43:57.260 --> 00:44:00.889
It was no small achievement,
B'Elanna.

00:44:00.930 --> 00:44:03.660
You gave that unit life.

00:44:06.669 --> 00:44:09.194
You should have seen it,
Captain.

00:44:09.239 --> 00:44:13.073
It was incredible.

00:44:13.109 --> 00:44:16.078
I installed that module

00:44:16.112 --> 00:44:19.275
and the prototype
looked up at me

00:44:19.315 --> 00:44:22.546
and asked me for programming.

00:44:26.089 --> 00:44:28.148
As I said,

00:44:28.191 --> 00:44:29.715
it must've been difficult.

00:44:34.397 --> 00:44:36.831
It was necessary.
